This software, together with its documentation, screenshots and build artifacts
(the "Work"), is entirely original work by the author — not a repost, not a
modification or repackaging of anyone else's software. It is published on an
"All Rights Reserved" basis: the public repository exists for transparency,
defect reporting and community collaboration, and grants no transfer of
copyright.

1. RIGHTS GRANTED (FREE FOREVER, NON-COMMERCIAL)

   You may:
   (a) download, install and run the Work free of charge on a personal device
       that you own outright and that carries no organisation-managed agent,
       for your own privacy and security self-checks;
   (b) view and fork this repository, and submit Pull Requests as described in
       CONTRIBUTING.md;
   (c) quote portions of the documentation, with attribution and a link to the
       original repository, for review, commentary or teaching.

   The Work is free forever. The author will not charge for it, will not offer
   any paid edition, and it will never pursue any commercial purpose.

2. PROHIBITED (WITHOUT PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION)

   You may not:
   (a) use the Work on equipment issued by an organisation, on devices
       connected to an organisation's network, or on any device subject to
       organisational management;
   (b) use the Work to circumvent, disable or defeat security controls,
       auditing, monitoring or data-protection measures lawfully deployed by
       any organisation;
   (c) sell, resell, rent or bundle the Work, make it part of a paid service,
       course or community, or otherwise monetise it directly or indirectly;
   (d) redistribute the Work or any modified version, paid or free;
   (e) modify, rename or de-attribute the Work and republish it, or publish
       derivative works based on it;
   (f) remove or alter the terms in this file, the README or DISCLAIMER.

3. ORIGINAL WORK

   The program name, interface, detection logic and remediation logic are the
   author's independent work. The Work contains no cracks, patches, keygens or
   unauthorised third-party code, and provides no capability to generate,
   build, drop or distribute trojans, viruses, worms, ransomware, keyloggers,
   stealers or backdoors, no ability to intrude on or control another person's
   device, and no function that violates the laws of the People's Republic of
   China.

4. CONTRIBUTIONS

   By having a Pull Request merged you grant the author a perpetual, worldwide,
   royalty-free, irrevocable licence to use, modify, sublicense and distribute
   your contribution in any manner, and you agree that your contribution is
   provided to third parties under the same terms as this file.

5. DISCLAIMER

   THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM
